  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper evaluates Variational Quantum Circuit classifiers for fraud detection using PCA‑reduced datasets (2–8 features, 1k–20k samples) derived from a 515,651‑transaction bank dataset with ~2% fraud rate. Across 400 trained models per dataset, simulated VQC models sometimes achieved higher precision‑recall scores than classical methods such as logistic regression and SVM, but experiments used only 2–8 qubits on a simulator and performance collapsed when run on real IBM hardware (ibm_brisbane), showing current devices are not yet practical for the task.",
  "experiments": [
